quest title=Water to the City
quest intro=A stone city with a dry fountain and an aqueduct across the lagoon. The water-master's decree is carved on the fountain.
step reach|citygate|1|Land at the harbour gate of Aquila
step read|The water-master's decree|1|Climb to the square and read the decree on the fountain
step reach|source|1|Climb the west peak to the source
step collect|story:valvekey|1|Take the valve key from the water-master's box
step collect|story:tally|1|Open valve one at the spring house
step reach|cistern|1|Climb down into the flooded cistern
step collect|story:tally|2|Dive to valve two on the cistern's floor
step kill|Screecher|2|Fight off the screechers on the arches
step collect|story:tally|3|Open valve three on the middle arch
step collect|story:tally|4|Open valve four in the sluice house
step collect|story:castellumkey|1|Find the castellum's key in the city's watch house
step collect|story:tally|5|Open valve five in the castellum
step reach|fountain|1|See the fountain run
step reach|treasury|1|Go into the treasury beside the fountain
step open|The city treasury|1|Open the city treasury
quest done=Water runs from the source to the city again, in every gutter and through the fountain's mouth. Aquila is alive - for as long as somebody keeps the valves.
quest reward=Mango*3;CopperIngot*2;Rope*3

save The Aqueduct
